y":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T22:04:30-08:00","id":1469229,"title":"","content":"I have done a thread on transforming some of our favorite fairytale characters and literary figures as high wyrd Changelings. My favorite is Edgar Allen Poe as a darkling author and his wife Eleanor has a fairest nymph.<br /> <br /> However, I found an image that gives an interesting idea for Eleanor as a Fairest Banshee kith.<br /> <br /> Here it is.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/genzoman/art/Lenore-892883788\" target=\"_blank\">Lenore by GENZOMAN on DeviantArt</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T22:10:40-08:00","id":1469230,"title":"","content":"This image would be an interesting portrayal of Edgar Allen Poe as a darkling author.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/fremuard/art/DoubleMEME-Ragamuffin-737396144\" target=\"_blank\">[DoubleMEME] Ragamuffin by Fremuard on DeviantArt</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T22:43:42-08:00","id":1469232,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/869426-changeling-inspirational-gallery?p=1469229#post1469229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite is Edgar Allen Poe as a darkling author and his wife Eleanor has a fairest nymph.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a little correction, Poe's wife was Virginia Clemm. Lenore is just a name he used twice for female characters in his poems, but he used others and the two specific poems aren't about his wife in any capacity.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Raven&quot; has little to do with any particular characteristic of the deceased Lenore in the poem, and &quot;Lenore&quot; was possibly inspired by the death of his brother. His actual wife was alive and well during both writings.<br /> <br /> But he did loved his wife too much, married when she was 13 (he was 27), and he died just 2 years after her, so take from it what you may about who's the most interesting character to have at his side...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-29T23:12:26-08:00","id":1469233,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/869426-changeling-inspirational-gallery?p=1469232#post1469232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a little correction, Poe's wife was Virginia Clemm. Lenore is just a name he used twice for female characters in his poems, but he used others and the two specific poems aren't about his wife in any capacity.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Raven&quot; has little to do with any particular characteristic of the deceased Lenore in the poem, and &quot;Lenore&quot; was possibly inspired by the death of his brother. His actual wife was alive and well during both writings.<br /> <br /> But he did loved his wife too much, married when she was 13 (he was 27), and he died just 2 years after her, so take from it what you may about who's the most interesting character to have at his side...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, But I think Edgar Allen Poe's two poems, <b><i>The Raven</i></b> and <b><i>Anna Belle Lee</i></b> both referred to his wife, Virginia Clemm. So in my chronicles, Poe calls his wife both Anna Belle Lee and Lenore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-30T16:17:49-08:00","id":1469278,"title":"","content":"As it is the Christmas season,<br /> <br /> Here is a picture of Krampus and Perchta.<b